{
  "id": "navier_stokes_equations",
  "title": "Navier-Stokes Equations",
  "description": "The Navier-Stokes equations are the fundamental partial differentials equations used to describe incompressible fluid flows. These equations describe incompressible fluid flow and are essential in computational fluid dynamics.",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Navier-Stokes Equations\n\nThe Navier-Stokes equations are the fundamental partial differential equations used to describe incompressible fluid flows.\n\n## Overview\nA theoretical introduction to The Navier-Stokes Equations. The Navier-Stokes Equations are the fundamental partial differentials equations describing incompressible fluid flow.\n\n## References\n- [Wolfram MathWorld - Navier-Stokes Equations](http://scienceworld.wolfram.com/physics/Navier-StokesEquations.html)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "headers": [
        "Input Parameters",
        "Values"
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "velocity_x",
          "label": "Velocity (X-component)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m/s",
          "defaultValue": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "velocity_y",
          "label": "Velocity (Y-component)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m/s",
          "defaultValue": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure",
          "label": "Pressure",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "defaultValue": 101325
        },
        {
          "id": "viscosity",
          "label": "Dynamic Viscosity",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa·s",
          "defaultValue": 0.001
        },
        {
          "id": "density",
          "label": "Fluid Density",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "defaultValue": 1000
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "kinematic_viscosity",
          "label": "Kinematic Viscosity",
          "formula": "inputs.viscosity / inputs.density",
          "unit": "m²/s",
          "format": "scientific"
        },
        {
          "id": "reynolds_number",
          "label": "Reynolds Number (characteristic)",
          "formula": "(inputs.density * Math.sqrt(inputs.velocity_x * inputs.velocity_x + inputs.velocity_y * inputs.velocity_y)) / inputs.viscosity",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Symbol",
        "Unit",
        "Description"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Velocity",
          "u, v, w",
          "m/s",
          "Flow velocity components in x, y, z directions"
        ],
        [
          "Pressure",
          "p",
          "Pa",
          "Fluid pressure"
        ],
        [
          "Density",
          "ρ",
          "kg/m³",
          "Fluid mass density"
        ],
        [
          "Dynamic Viscosity",
          "μ",
          "Pa·s",
          "Measure of fluid resistance to shear stress"
        ],
        [
          "Kinematic Viscosity",
          "ν",
          "m²/s",
          "Ratio of dynamic viscosity to density"
        ],
        [
          "External Force",
          "f",
          "N/m³",
          "Body forces per unit volume"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "options": {
        "title": {
          "text": "Velocity Field Visualization",
          "left": "center"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "trigger": "axis"
        },
        "xAxis": {
          "type": "category",
          "data": [
            "Low Re",
            "Moderate Re",
            "High Re",
            "Turbulent"
          ]
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "type": "value",
          "name": "Flow Characteristics"
        },
        "series": [
          {
            "name": "Viscous Effects",
            "type": "line",
            "data": [
              95,
              75,
              40,
              15
            ],
            "smooth": true
          },
          {
            "name": "Inertial Effects",
            "type": "line",
            "data": [
              5,
              25,
              60,
              85
            ],
            "smooth": true
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}